This project is a Next.js monolith — an admin-only tool that:
1. Takes book topic text as input (Class > Subject > Chapter > Topic hierarchy)
2. Chunks the text and embeds it into pgvector (for RAG)
3. Lets you test RAG retrieval + AI answers in a playground
4. Lets you hand-write, review, and export Q&A datasets for fine-tuning
5. Triggers and tracks training jobs (actual training runs in a separate Python service)

Rules:
- Use App Router (/app), not Pages Router
- All DB access through Prisma; raw SQL only for pgvector queries ($queryRaw)
- API routes live under /app/api, business logic lives in /lib (keep route.ts thin)
- Server Components by default, "use client" only when interactivity is needed
- UI with Tailwind + shadcn/ui, avoid custom CSS
- Code/variable names always in English
- No student-facing features for now — admin/internal tool only
- Keep DATABASE_URL, SESSION_SECRET, OLLAMA_BASE_URL, OLLAMA_EMBEDDING_MODEL in .env
